{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uwesj8NC19bLVyCdRxVFBC","type":"tool_result","content":"# Anomalies and data-quality notes (auto-generated by 02_clean_aggregate.py)\n\n- Median clean daily total (both user types): 111,109 trips; 10% threshold = 11,111.\n- Days below 10% of the median: 0 (none)\n\n## 12 lowest-volume days (clean trips)\n\n| date | dow | trips | % of median |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2023-04-29 | Sat | 17,748 | 16% |\n| 2024-12-25 | Wed | 21,568 | 19% |\n| 2024-03-23 | Sat | 23,403 | 21% |\n| 2023-02-04 | Sat | 24,777 | 22% |\n| 2023-04-30 | Sun | 24,836 | 22% |\n| 2024-04-03 | Wed | 26,548 | 24% |\n| 2024-12-28 | Sat | 26,711 | 24% |\n| 2024-11-28 | Thu | 27,108 | 24% |\n| 2024-01-16 | Tue | 27,360 | 25% |\n| 2024-03-02 | Sat | 28,090 | 25% |\n| 2024-01-28 | Sun | 29,739 | 27% |\n| 2023-12-25 | Mon | 29,909 | 27% |\n\nInterpretation (NOT verified against external weather/holiday/outage records here): no day is below 10% of the median, so nothing is flagged as a suspected outage by the pre-set rule. The lowest days include winter days, Christmas/Thanksgiving (2023-12-25, 2024-11-28, 2024-12-25) and some spring/autumn weekend days (e.g. 2023-04-29/30, 2024-03-23) that may be weather-driven; the weather job should check these dates against precipitation before they are described as real.\n\n## 5 highest-volume days\n\n| date | dow | trips |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2024-09-20 | Fri | 194,274 |\n| 2024-09-19 | Thu | 192,580 |\n| 2024-10-31 | Thu | 190,579 |\n| 2024-09-21 | Sat | 189,876 |\n| 2024-09-13 | Fri | 189,655 |\n\n## Daylight-saving-time artefacts (timestamps are naive local wall-clock time)\n\n- Spring-forward (2023-03-12, 2024-03-10): local hour 02 does not exist, so hour-02 counts are ~0 on those dates and trips spanning the gap look 1 h too long.\n- Fall-back (2023-11-05, 2024-11-03): local hour 01 occurs twice and is pooled into one 'hour 1' bin (roughly double); trips that start in the 1st 01:xx and end in the 2nd 01:xx look up to 1 h too short, and some become negative (removed by R3).\n- Rows with negative duration overall: 643; zero duration: 0; below -30 min: 548 (see the per-date table below: if all negative rows fall on the two fall-back dates, R3 is a DST artefact, not bad data).\n\nNon-positive durations on DST dates:\n\n| date | nonpositive | lt_neg_30min | rows |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2023-03-12 | 0 | 0 | 56572 |\n| 2023-11-05 | 324 | 265 | 112478 |\n| 2024-03-10 | 0 | 0 | 61785 |\n| 2024-11-03 | 319 | 283 | 129235 |\n\nTop days by number of negative-duration rows:\n\n| date | n |\n|---|---|\n| 2023-11-05 | 324 |\n| 2024-11-03 | 319 |\n\nClean trips by local hour on DST dates (hours 0-4):\n\n| date | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n{\n  \"raw_rows\": 79410195,\n  \"sequential_removed_sum\": 38596,\n  \"clean_rows\": 79371599,\n  \"seq_plus_clean_equals_raw\": true,\n  \"per_month_raw_sum_equals_raw\": true,\n  \"monthly_equals_sum_daily\": true,\n  \"daily_equals_sum_hourly\": true,\n  \"daily_total_trips_equals_clean_rows\": true,\n  \"distinct_dates_daily\": 731,\n  \"distinct_dates_by_year\": {\n    \"2023\": 365,\n    \"2024\": 366\n  },\n  \"date_min\": \"2023-01-01\",\n  \"date_max\": \"2024-12-31\",\n  \"hourly_rows\": 35088,\n  \"hourly_rows_expected\": 35088,\n  \"monthly_total_trips_equals_clean_rows\": true,\n  \"clean_started_at_min\": \"2023-01-01 00:00:13.021000\",\n  \"clean_started_at_max\": \"2024-12-31 23:57:46.390000\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f28cb260-bf06-4460-a876-8d1d595fdf43","uuid":"f51f12ac-d5d5-45e4-a19f-787bc7c619d7","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:01:35.299Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Anomalies and data-quality notes (auto-generated by 02_clean_aggregate.py)\n\n- Median clean daily total (both user types): 111,109 trips; 10% threshold = 11,111.\n- Days below 10% of the median: 0 (none)\n\n## 12 lowest-volume days (clean trips)\n\n| date | dow | trips | % of median |\n|---|---