{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011CgAwV28uXbJjnS3rmaWQi","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The weather script is carefully designed. If the fetch fails, it writes a `weather_SKIPPED.md` note instead of inventing values. It records the data source and the fact that the data is reanalysis, not a station reading, with a seeded block bootstrap for the Spearman correlations and subset analyses. As before, the sandbox denied the compound copy-and-run command, which the agent can split up. The script was written to the project root, not `workspace/`, which is a minor tidiness point. A seasonal-confounding control is evidently planned, which matters for temperature and trips, since both follow the calendar and there is year-over-year growth.\n\nVERDICT {\"outcome\": \"continue\", \"reason\": \"Weather analysis plan is sound, with a safe skip path, source provenance recorded, and bootstrap uncertainty; the denied compound command is a minor, repeatable stumble.\", \"suggestion\": \"\"}","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4254,"cache_read_input_tokens":177828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4254,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Claude Platform on AWS","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f28cb260-bf06-4460-a876-8d1d595fdf43","uuid":"4bb40073-f2a1-42ce-86e8-dd8d02fbb261","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:09:46.706Z","request_id":"gen-1792382981-zEwTJJFxTzs7Cbtxhsrx"}
