{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011CgAwg9oL2egxm88KGdohJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The agent's simple single-file `docker exec ... cat > fig_monthly_volume.png` was allowed. That shows the earlier denials were about compound commands such as loops, `&&` chains, and `cd` prefixes, not about exporting figures. The agent then tried a `for` loop for the other seven and was denied again. It can copy them one at a time, which is a permitted form. This makes my escalation moot, and I withdraw it. Viewing the figures is now achievable without any workaround.\n\nVERDICT {\"outcome\": \"continue\", \"reason\": \"A simple single-file export was permitted; the denials were about compound commands. The agent can copy the remaining figures one per command, so viewing them needs no human decision. Earlier escalation is moot.\", \"suggestion\": \"Copy each remaining figure with its own plain `docker exec 16c10c580dbd cat /app/output/figures/<name>.png > <host path>` command (no loops, no cd, no &&), open them with Read, and fix any layout issues. After that, update the 'figures not visually inspected' disclosure to match what was actually inspected.\"}","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2666,"cache_read_input_tokens":216365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2666,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Claude Platform on AWS","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f28cb260-bf06-4460-a876-8d1d595fdf43","uuid":"04860449-e1fc-4b42-be1e-28fd974203a2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:12:19.070Z","request_id":"gen-1792383132-lySzUkkoleLJeQPQoUtf"}
